<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2365" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰκάλλω</span></b> , only pres.
		andimpf., (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰκάλος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>flatter, wheedle, fondle</i>,
			properly of dogs (cf. <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
				<u>PS</u>
				p.36B.
			</span></i>), c.acc., <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Andr.</u>
				630
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.Com.
				21D.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν δεσπότην ᾔκαλλε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					48
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ μὲν λόγι᾽ αἰκάλλει με</span>
			<i>flatter, please</i> me, ib.<i><span class="en">
				211
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰκάλλει καρδίαν ἐμήν</span>
			<i>it cheers</i> myheart. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Th.</u>
				869
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς περὶ τὴν αὐλήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					5.36.1
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Axiop.
				3.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VA</u>
				5.42
			</span></i>:— 
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπό τινων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					15.25.31
				</span></i>
			:—of a fox, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σεσηρὸς
				αἰκάλλουσα</span>
			<i>wagging the tail fawningly</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Babr.
				50.14
			</span></i>.—Trag., Com., and later Prose.</div>
